# Deprecated CLI translation benchmark — corpus CONTENT is never tracked.
# This whole tree is deprecated (see DEPRECATED.md) and unused by `npm test`.
# The data it holds is corpus content and must stay out of git (corpora are
# fetch-from-source; ANY license is blocked — see scripts/quarantine_gate.sh).
#
#   fixtures/       FLORES-200 devtest sentences, one file per language. Split
#                   across files (monolingual {id,text}), so EN is the source
#                   and every other language a reference — together a parallel
#                   corpus. CC-BY-SA, still corpus content → never tracked.
#   results/raw/    Per-model FLORES translations ({"translations":{"0":…}}) —
#                   the translated other side of that corpus → never tracked.
#   content-bench/  scraped third-party commercial website text (Apple, Airbnb,
#                   …) aligned EN<->locale — copyrighted, archived negative result.
#   ui-bench/       Signal Desktop UI localization strings (EN -> de/es/fr/ja/ko/zh).
#
# Regenerate locally with the scrape/extract scripts (kept tracked). Stats,
# config, READMEs and scripts stay tracked; only the parallel text is de-hosted.
# (flores-metadata.json = id/word_count/category only, no text → stays tracked;
#  results/costs.json + results/benchmark.log = run stats only → stay tracked.)
fixtures/flores-devtest.*.json
results/raw/
content-bench/raw/
content-bench/source/
content-bench/reference/
ui-bench/source/
ui-bench/reference/
